      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Currently working on detecting gestures using finger positions from VRCPlayerApi.GetBonePosition and GetBoneRotation. And it's inconsistent. Some avatars have neutral and open hand positions that are too similar to distinguish. Some fist poses have very different thumb positions. And some avatars have nonstandard hand poses. (often instead of rock n' roll)\n\nAccessing gestures directly would be much more robust.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-31T16:47:45.473Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Udon World Hand Gestures or Capacitive Buttons\n\nCurrent there is no way for Udon to know what gesture a given player is making with their hand. \n\nIf avatar gestures were to be exposed to Udon for the purpose of using them for world events triggers, world builder could use player hand gestures to interact with the world. In addition, combining player's Avatar hand gestures with the motion and position of the hand can allow for an infinite amount of interesting world interactions. \n\nFor example a player could hold their open hand gesture out in front of them to create and energy shield, and make a fist gesture and punch forward to create an energy blast of varying power depending on the velocity of the controller's movement. \n\nWe do have access to thumb stick positions, triggers and grip buttons presses, and A, B, X, Y button presses but do not have access to capacitive button touch which some gestures rely on. Allowing Udon to access capacitive buttons will allow world builders to create systems that could mimic the VRChat gesture system, but the best solution would be to send the given gestures straight through from player avatar to world Udon.\n\nThank you,\n\nZorgy",
